# 9. POWERSHELL COMMANDS REFERENCE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

Always end responses with the relevant command(s) from this list:

Run Flutter app in Chrome:
```powershell
cd C:\Users\user\Desktop\paragon
flutter run -d chrome
```

Build and deploy to Firebase Hosting:
```powershell
cd C:\Users\user\Desktop\paragon
flutter build web --release
firebase deploy --only hosting
```

Deploy Firestore rules only:
```powershell
cd C:\Users\user\Desktop\paragon
firebase deploy --only firestore:rules
```

Deploy Firestore indexes only:
```powershell
cd C:\Users\user\Desktop\paragon
firebase deploy --only firestore:indexes
```

Run the full scraper pipeline (from tools/scraper/):
```powershell
cd C:\Users\user\Desktop\paragon\tools\scraper
node 1_scrape.js
node 2_classify.js
node fix_misclassified.js
# spot check classified.json here
node 3_seed.js
```

Git push:
```powershell
cd C:\Users\user\Desktop\paragon
git add .
git commit -m "your message here"
git push
```

Add a Flutter package:
```powershell
cd C:\Users\user\Desktop\paragon
flutter pub add <package_name>
```

If firebase CLI stops working:
```powershell
C:\Users\user\AppData\Roaming\npm\firebase.cmd deploy --only hosting
```

If flutterfire CLI stops working — add to System PATH permanently:
  C:\Users\user\AppData\Local\Pub\Cache\bin


