# 12. SESSION CONTEXT (current as of post-Session 10)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

Session 8 is done: Physics (1769 questions) and Further Mathematics (801 questions)
scraped, classified, fixed, and seeded — all three launch subjects are now live.

Since Session 8, unplanned work has also landed outside the numbered plan below:
sign-in rebuilt as a multi-step email flow from Figma, the welcome screen rebuilt
from Figma, and the theme reconciled with Figma tokens (Space Grotesk, AppColors
palette). None of this maps to a specific session number — treat `git log` as the
source of truth for exactly what's shipped, not this file's session numbering alone.

Session 9 is done, but scoped down from the original one-liner: "video embed +
notes per topic" assumed video/notes content that does not exist anywhere —
Topic docs, topics.json, and questions.explanation are all empty of it, live,
for every seeded topic and question. What shipped instead is the navigational
and rendering shell: LearnScreen (route
`/subject/:subjectId/unit/:unitId/topic/:topicId/learn`), a Learn/Practice
button pair on TopicListScreen, `Topic.hasNotes`/`Topic.notesMarkdown` (nullable,
null-safe, unused by any current doc), and a first real use of the
already-pinned `connectivity_plus` dependency for the offline state
(`core/providers/connectivity_provider.dart`). No video player package was
added — there's no `videoId` for one to ever play. See `docs/audit/NEXT.md`
for what this intentionally leaves open (notes-authoring path, real Markdown
rendering, worked examples, video embedding).

Session 10 is done, scoped to exactly what was named: setup screen + exam
lockdown, plus the guest auth flow (called out as in-scope this session,
bigger-scope option chosen explicitly). What shipped: `WaecExamSetupScreen`
(year-range slider bounded by each subject's real min/max year — queried
live via `waecYearRangeProvider`, not hardcoded — question-count slider with
a live `count()` availability label that auto-snaps the count down if the
selected range can't fill it, timer toggle+duration, shuffle toggle),
`WaecExamScreen` rewritten to take its question set as route `extra`
(`WaecExamSessionData`) instead of querying Firestore itself, a real
per-second countdown with 5-min/1-min haptic cues and auto-submit at zero,
an exit-confirmation dialog, and Firebase Anonymous Auth wired end-to-end
(`signInAnonymously`, `isGuestProvider`, a "Browse as Guest" entry point on
the welcome screen, router redirect updated so a guest can still reach
`/welcome`/`/signin` to upgrade, and guest restrictions on the WAEC subject
list — locked to Mathematics — and setup screen — timer forced off, shuffle
forced on and hidden, upsell chip to sign in).

Live-verified in browser as a real signed-in user end to end: subject
unlock/lock, every setup control (including the auto-snap and the live
per-subject year range — Further Mathematics correctly shows 2006-2025, not
a hardcoded range), the countdown ticking in real time, the exit dialog, the
submit-confirmation dialog's unanswered-count, the results screen, and
attempt persistence (10 answered questions round-tripped to Firestore and
were confirmed present before cleanup).

Guest sign-in was initially blocked by Anonymous Authentication being
disabled in the Firebase Console — confirmed independently via the Identity
Toolkit REST API before anyone touched app code, and fixed by enabling it
in the Console (Authentication → Sign-in method → Anonymous). Once
unblocked, live-verified in browser as a fresh guest end to end: (1)
"Browse as Guest" issues a real UID and creates `users/{uid}` with
`isAnonymous: true`; (2) the WAEC subject list locks Further Maths/Physics
with the "Sign in to choose your subject" snackbar and leaves Mathematics
open; (3) the setup screen shows a locked "Untimed" timer, hides the
shuffle toggle entirely, and renders the upsell chip; (4) a 10-question
guest exam submitted cleanly and all 10 attempts round-tripped to Firestore
with `source: 'waec'` and the guest's UID; (5) signing out and browsing as
guest again issues a brand-new random UID — the previous guest's
`users/{uid}` doc and attempts remain in Firestore but are permanently
orphaned, with no UI path back to them (consistent with no account-linking
existing yet, see deferred items below).

Two real bugs surfaced and fixed during that live pass, both within scope
of this session's own code (not pre-existing):
- `users/{uid}` was never written with an `isAnonymous` field at all
  (`UserRepository.createUserIfNew`) — fixed, now set from `user.isAnonymous`
  on creation.
- The router's own guest-permissive redirect (added this session so a guest
  revisiting `/welcome`/`/signin` to upgrade isn't bounced home) had the
  side effect of also leaving a *freshly* signed-in guest stranded on
  `/welcome` — the redirect has no way to distinguish "just signed in,
  should land on home" from "already a guest, revisiting to upgrade,
  should stay put." Fixed by making `_handleGuestSignIn` navigate to `/`
  explicitly after `signInAnonymously` succeeds, rather than relying on the
  router to do it. Google/email sign-in were never affected (those become
  "really signed in," which the existing redirect rule already handles).

Deferred out of this session's stated scope (setup + lockdown only) — see
`docs/audit/NEXT.md`: the Auth Upsell Sheet / `linkWithCredential`
account-linking path (spec §2.1.10 vs §2.3.11 self-contradiction, resolved
here by choosing the simpler no-linking interpretation), guest-gating on
Dashboard/Drill/Profile screens (only WAEC was in scope), a
`sessions/{examId}` collection plus `/exam/results`/`/exam/review`/`/exam/history`
routes, mid-exam local persistence/resume (`shared_preferences` isn't a
dependency yet), question flagging, and the deliberate `setState` +
`Timer.periodic` deviation from the spec's literal `StateNotifier` wording.

Unnumbered pass after Session 10 — the answer key. Every one of the 4,286
seeded questions had `correctIndex: null` and an empty `explanation`, so no
answer a student picked could ever be marked correct: drill turned every
submission red, every exam scored 0%, and the whole `attempts` corpus was
100% `isCorrect: false`. Live breakage in shipped code, and it silently
blocked Sessions 12 and 13 (accuracy and XP over a corpus where nothing is
correct) as well as any results/review screen.

The answers were never scraped — `1_scrape.js` hardcodes `correctIndex: null`
— but they were still available from the same source. `4_scrape_answers.js`
crawls them from `__NUXT_DATA__` (myschool.ng is a Nuxt app now, so the old
`.question-item` selectors match nothing), and `5_match_answers.js` joins
them onto the existing docs on normalized question text, since the seeder
never stored a source id. Backfilled `correctIndex`, `explanation`,
`sourceId` and `hasAnswer` for **4,254 of 4,286 (99.3%)**.

Three things worth remembering from it:
- **Stored years were clean.** 0 wrong out of 4,254, so `1_scrape.js` never
  hit the trap the new crawler did — the site silently serves a different
  year when it doesn't stock the one requested, which is why the new crawler
  reads `collection.exam_year` from the payload instead of trusting the URL.
- **The key is not authoritative.** Hand-verifying 60 answers from the oldest
  years found 2 wrong at source (~4% of the verifiable sample); the site
  describes its own answers as AI-assisted. Question flagging shipped
  alongside for exactly this reason. No UI string claims answers are
  verified or official, and that should stay true.
- **32 questions still have no verified answer** and are filtered out of
  drill and WAEC by `hasAnswer`, rather than left in circulation where they
  would always be marked wrong.

Phase 3 build sessions (planned):
  9   Learn mode — video embed + notes per topic ✅ done (shell only, see above)
  10  Proper exam mode — configurable settings, lockdown ✅ done (see above; guest flow fully live-verified after two in-session bugs were fixed)
